        "id": 3495154,
        "postDate": "2026-07-11T14:43:46.227Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "This is the kind of tool sharing that moves a competition forward. Most public notebooks are just clones.\n\n3D trajectory and frame to frame matching is the debugging step people skip, then wonder why their tracking model scores fine but looks wrong visually. Metrics on cell tracking can look okay while the actual trajectories are jumping between cells.\n\nDoes it handle two cells crossing paths where the model swaps their IDs? That failure is invisible in aggregate scores and obvious the second you watch the video.",
        "content": "<p>This is the kind of tool sharing that moves a competition forward. Most public notebooks are just clones.</p>\n<p>3D trajectory and frame to frame matching is the debugging step people skip, then wonder why their tracking model scores fine but looks wrong visually. Metrics on cell tracking can look okay while the actual trajectories are jumping between cells.</p>\n<p>Does it handle two cells crossing paths where the model swaps their IDs? That failure is invisible in aggregate scores and obvious the second you watch the video.</p>",
